roup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"integer","year":2015,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l132nezo","chapter":"coordination-compounds","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-1-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"pfor-the-octahedral-complexes-of-fesup3sup-in-scnsu-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-98csnwc0hcejmwvs","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>For the octahedral complexes of Fe<sup>3+</sup> in SCN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> (thiocyana-to-S) and in CN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> ligand environments, the difference between the spin-only magnetic moments in Bohr magnetons (when approximated to the nearest integer) is __________.</p>\n<p>[Atomic number Fe = 26]</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"4","explanation":"<p>The spin only magnetic moment is given by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.639ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.061ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.5 6657 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(880.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(1936.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,67.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(1020,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(989,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1811.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2811.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3311.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"3700.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"1020\" y=\"857.5\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, where n is the number of unpaired electrons.</p>\n<p>Fe<sup>3+</sup> complex with weak field ligand SCN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> contains five unpaired electrons.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 39 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l14ehvh5/756cb51e-812a-422c-b090-ae302433b7a2/a8d00890-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14ehvh6.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Therefore, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = 5.9 BM.</p>\n<p>Fe<sup>3+</sup> complex with strong field ligand CN<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> contains one unpaired electron.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 39 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l14eikhv/dddda4d8-358c-4936-af34-655b3465c680/bc23d930-ab1d-11ec-aac4-3998acfb8613/file-1l14eikhw.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Therefore, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = 1.73 BM.</p>\n<p>Thus, the difference in spin only magnetic moment is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.124ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"0.968ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -483 778 428\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"224